#
# Purpose:
#   cebe/php-openapi 1.8.0 (the latest tagged release, May 2025) declares
#   several parameters with the implicit-nullable shape
#   `Type $param = null`. PHP 8.4 deprecates that syntax and every consumer
#   sees the notice. Upstream has not moved since 1.8.0, and paogen ADR-008
#   keeps us on cebe's 3.0 parser for v0.1, so we apply a local patch that
#   adds the explicit `?` on each affected signature.
#
# Upstream: https://github.com/php-openapi/php-openapi
#           (was https://github.com/cebe/php-openapi, redirected)
#
# Drop this patch when:
#   - a tagged cebe/php-openapi release ships these signatures with
#     explicit `?Type` (or equivalent), and composer.json pins that
#     release; OR
#   - paogen swaps parsers (see truth/decisions/008-openapi-31-strategy.typ).
#
# Scope (9 signatures):
#   src/SpecBaseObject.php:396       resolveReferences(?ReferenceContext ...)
#   src/SpecObjectInterface.php:43   resolveReferences(?ReferenceContext ...)
